Draft patch — PR #157 reset-mail transport (CONFIRMED narrowed residual, verdicts.md item 46). transport_for_actor exempted the person's default workspace from the owner requirement, and default_workspace() is chosen-or-earliest-JOINED — so reset/confirmation tokens could transit SMTP controlled by another workspace's owner, contradicting the function's own doc comment. Requires role='owner' for every candidate (the default-first ORDER BY is unchanged and now only ranks owned workspaces;  remains bound for it). Uncompiled in the authoring sandbox; land WITH a Postgres integration test (owner/member x default/non-default x mail on/off).

